[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mSeal Healthy Local Cluster Runtime Contract\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Deliver epic `VFH7YspJx` so the shipped local single-node cluster lane boots live, reports healthy status, returns a usable kubeconfig handoff, and fixes the packaged guest-artifact validation path. (\u001b[2mVFH7YspJx\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - The checked-in example succeeds on Linux with `port --config examples/port.toml cluster up --cluster demo --runtime-root <tmp> --format json` instead of failing during Firecracker boot. (\u001b[2mrun the shipped local cluster workflow on Linux and confirm `cluster up` succeeds\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-03\u001b[0m - `port cluster status --format json` reports `readiness=ready`, `machine_state=running`, and `kubeconfig_available=true`, and `port cluster kubeconfig --format json` plus `kubectl get nodes -o wide` works without kubeconfig rewriting. (\u001b[2minspect live local cluster status and kubeconfig handoff with downstream tooling\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-04\u001b[0m - `port --config examples/port.toml artifacts validate --artifact demo-guest --architecture x86-64` succeeds from the installed or packaged CLI contract instead of resolving validation scripts under `/build/...`. (\u001b[2mrun the shipped artifact validate path outside a source-build-only assumption\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-05\u001b[0m - Scope stays single-node local only; no AWS, hosted cluster, or multi-node expansion lands in this mission. (\u001b[2mreview planning and implementation artifacts for explicit single-node local boundaries\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVFH7YspJx\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Ship Bootable Local Cluster Guest And Artifact Lane (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-03-29T09:42:14\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VFH7XN6Fi/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Seal Healthy Local Cluster Runtime Contract - Charter\r\n\r\nArchetype: Strategic\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Deliver epic `VFH7YspJx` so the shipped local single-node cluster lane boots live, reports healthy status, returns a usable kubeconfig handoff, and fixes the packaged guest-artifact validation path. | board: VFH7YspJx |\r\n| MG-02 | The checked-in example succeeds on Linux with `port --config examples/port.toml cluster up --cluster demo --runtime-root <tmp> --format json` instead of failing during Firecracker boot. | manual: run the shipped local cluster workflow on Linux and confirm `cluster up` succeeds |\r\n| MG-03 | `port cluster status --format json` reports `readiness=ready`, `machine_state=running`, and `kubeconfig_available=true`, and `port cluster kubeconfig --format json` plus `kubectl get nodes -o wide` works without kubeconfig rewriting. | manual: inspect live local cluster status and kubeconfig handoff with downstream tooling |\r\n| MG-04 | `port --config examples/port.toml artifacts validate --artifact demo-guest --architecture x86-64` succeeds from the installed or packaged CLI contract instead of resolving validation scripts under `/build/...`. | manual: run the shipped artifact validate path outside a source-build-only assumption |\r\n| MG-05 | Scope stays single-node local only; no AWS, hosted cluster, or multi-node expansion lands in this mission. | manual: review planning and implementation artifacts for explicit single-node local boundaries |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Fix runtime and artifact correctness, not proof UX, recorder migration, or broader docs polish.\r\n- Do not shift cluster bootstrap or kubeconfig handoff back onto downstream `guest exec`, join-token choreography, or manual kubeconfig rewriting.\r\n- Keep the mission bounded to the shipped single-node local cluster lane and packaged artifact path; defer AWS and multi-node expansion.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while the shipped local `cluster up/status/kubeconfig` workflow or packaged `artifacts validate` path still fail in the repo.\r\n- HALT when epic `VFH7YspJx` is done and manual verification confirms a live healthy local cluster handoff plus install-safe guest artifact validation.\r\n- YIELD if the remaining blocker requires a product decision on guest image provenance, Firecracker lane ownership, or downstream contract scope rather than implementation work.\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VFH7YspJx\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mShip Bootable Local Cluster Guest And Artifact Lane\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-29 09:38:15\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-03-29 09:48:13\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-29 11:30:09\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-03-29 11:30:09\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m1h 41m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFH7YspJx/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFH7YspJx/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  The previously verified cluster mission closed on operator surface and proof\r\n  criteria, but the shipped local single-node cluster lane is still not live.\r\n  <tmp> --format json` currently fails on Linux because Firecracker exits during\r\n  boot and the guest console ends in an ext4 checksum error followed by `Requested\r\n  artifacts validate --artifact demo-guest --architecture x86-64` still fails\r\n  under the installed CLI contract because the validation path resolves\r\n  \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mvalidate-guest-image.sh\u001b[0m under \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61m/build/...\u001b[0m instead of a shipped runtime-safe\r\n  location.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Boot the shipped single-node local cluster example successfully on Linux. (\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport ... cluster up --cluster demo --runtime-root <tmp> --format json\u001b[0m exits successfully and returns live launch output. -> The checked-in example works on a Linux development host without patching downstream repos.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Hand off a healthy cluster directly through Port surfaces. (\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcluster status --format json\u001b[0m reports readiness=\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mready\u001b[0m, machine_state=\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mrunning\u001b[0m, kubeconfig_available=\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mtrue\u001b[0m, and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcluster kubeconfig --format json\u001b[0m works with \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mkubectl get nodes -o wide\u001b[0m. -> Downstream tooling can consume the returned kubeconfig without manual rewrite.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Make the shipped guest artifact lane install-safe. (\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61martifacts validate --artifact demo-guest --architecture x86-64\u001b[0m succeeds from the packaged or installed Port contract. -> The validate path no longer depends on build-time-only \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61m/build/...\u001b[0m script locations.)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - The shipped \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mexamples/port.toml\u001b[0m local cluster workflow must boot a real single-node cluster through \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport cluster up\u001b[0m on Linux.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFH7t3cG9\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport cluster status\u001b[0m and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport cluster kubeconfig\u001b[0m must hand off a live healthy cluster without downstream kubeconfig rewriting or extra guest exec choreography.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFH7t3cG9\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - The shipped guest artifact validate path must resolve validation scripts and dependencies from install-safe locations rather than source-build-only paths.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFH7t3cG9\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - Keep scope bounded to the single-node local cluster lane and preserve explicit rejection or deferral of AWS and multi-node expansion.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (2): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFH7t3cG9\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m, \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFH7t3cG9\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Fix correctness and installability rather than compensating with extra docs, recorder work, or downstream glue.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFH7t3cG9\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-03\u001b[39m - Maintain Port ownership of bootstrap, health, and kubeconfig handoff once the lane is healthy.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFH7t3cG9\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              4/4 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m4/4\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Area: Method\r\n    - Cluster handoff: Live CLI run plus downstream \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mkubectl get nodes -o wide\u001b[0m using the returned kubeconfig\r\n    - Downstream consumption: Cross-repo manual verification in \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mspoke infra\u001b[0m\r\n    - Local cluster boot: Live CLI run on Linux plus runtime logs\r\n    - Packaged artifact validate: Installed or packaged CLI invocation of \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61martifacts validate\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 0 | manual 8\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 0 | manual 7\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 22 | media 0 | other 0\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFH7t3cG9\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Boot Live Local Cluster And Fix Packaged Guest Validation (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
